 "intro": "Outside the Colline Gate of Rome, 1 November 82 BC, at the end of the civil war between Sulla and the followers of Marius. The Samnites under Pontius Telesinus, with Marian and Lucanian forces, are at the walls. You are Lucius Cornelius Sulla.",
 "debrief": "In Plutarch’s and Appian’s accounts, Sulla attacked late in the afternoon against advice. His own left wing was broken and pushed back to the walls, where the defenders dropped the gate. Sulla himself was nearly killed. The fighting went on into the night until a messenger brought word that Marcus Crassus had routed the enemy on the right. At dawn the Samnites were destroyed and Telesinus was found dying. Sulla had thousands of prisoners killed while the Senate listened nearby, and began his proscriptions. The other choices are what-ifs.",
